00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.060
Here's something
you may not know.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.090
The Docs apps on desktop,
iOS, and Android,

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:52.770
actually work offline.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:56.220
And when you make edits offline,
and you come back online,

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:59.766
we will actually do a merge
of the edits you did offline

00:07:59.766 --> 00:08:02.140
with the edits that were done
by the other collaborators.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:05.602
It's pretty-- it's pretty cool.

00:08:05.602 --> 00:08:07.560
You might be seeing
something interesting here,

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.020
which is we're
actually assigning

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:12.990
action items to specific
people on your team.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.660
It turns out that people
spend a lot of time

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.500
at work tracking down
colleagues to get work done--

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.260
to just ask them to
follow up on small tasks.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.420
In fact, research has
shown that people spend up

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:27.270
to 20% of their work
week just doing this.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.970
That's about an entire day.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.610
So we've added intelligence
to Google Docs.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:37.030
You'll notice here that as
I type Ryan Weber to review

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:43.280
overall proposal, or Allen
Yang to check in with legal,

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:47.330
Docs intelligently suggests
action items on the side.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.880
We've detected the
